<title>ROMANIA: Romania c.bank cuts minimum rate to 190 pct vs 205.</title>
<headline>Romania c.bank cuts minimum rate to 190 pct vs 205.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's central bank (BNR) said on Thursday it had cut the minimum permitted rate for its auctioned funds to 190 percent from 205 percent last week.</p>
<p>The BNR kept one-week refinancing funds on offer flat at 300 billion lei.</p>
<p>Traders said short-term rates, which opened near 180 percent on a cash-heavy money market, were expected to slip to about 170 percent or even lower.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
